# Published configuration: lerobot/smolvla_base, 1 camera at 256x256 (256 SigLIP tokens, 65-token prefix).
# Sourced by run.sh after infra/env.sh (so SHVLA_DATA is set). Plain shell, no side effects.

# --- checkpoint (run.sh published fetch) ---
SHVLA_CKPT_ID="lerobot/smolvla_base"
SHVLA_CKPT_REV="5e8d12a6e2975b0e5e5fce7c8caf47c371d257b6"
export SHVLA_SMOLVLA_DIR="$SHVLA_DATA/smolvla_base"

# --- golden reference (infra/lerobot/golden_ref.py; written by hand, G2.1) ---
SHVLA_GOLDEN_OBS="synthetic:1:256:0"
SHVLA_GOLDEN="$SHVLA_DATA/golden/published.npz"

# --- host prepare commands, in order (run.sh published prepare) ---
# Each entry: "<softhier_mlir.frontend module> <arguments>", run as `python -m softhier_mlir.frontend.<module> ...`.
# D = $SHVLA_SMOLVLA_DIR, C = --ckpt $D/model.safetensors, R = $SHVLA_GOLDEN.
# SHVLA_PREPARE_OUT[i] is the file step i writes (size is reported).
_D="$SHVLA_SMOLVLA_DIR"
_C="--ckpt $_D/model.safetensors"
_R="$SHVLA_GOLDEN"
SHVLA_PREPARE_STEPS=(
    "smolvla prepare $_C --seq 256 --out $_D/vision_s256.npz"                 # rung 3
    "smolvla prepare $_C --seq 1024 --out $_D/vision_s1024.npz"               # the chain's SigLIP weights (every token count)
    "smolvla prepare-vlm $_C --cams 1 --out $_D/vlm_c1.npz"
    "smolvla_expert prepare $_C --ref $_R --out $_D/expert.npz"               # needs the golden reference
    "smolvla_e2e prepare $_C --ref $_R --out $_D/e2e_c1_t256.npz"             # needs the golden reference
)
SHVLA_PREPARE_OUT=(
    "$_D/vision_s256.npz" "$_D/vision_s1024.npz" "$_D/vlm_c1.npz" "$_D/expert.npz" "$_D/e2e_c1_t256.npz"
)
unset _D _C _R

# --- expected stage times, simulated ms (softhier-mlir docs/SMOLVLA_E2E.md table, lines 117-123: vision 27.32, prefix 14.80, expert 76.70, total 119.10; connector 0.28 as listed in the design) ---
SHVLA_EXPECT_TOTAL_MS="119.1"
SHVLA_EXPECT_VISION_MS="27.3"
SHVLA_EXPECT_CONNECTOR_MS="0.28"
SHVLA_EXPECT_PREFIX_MS="14.8"
SHVLA_EXPECT_EXPERT_MS="76.7"

# Owner-approved exception only: raise the per-simulator-process limit (seconds). Default 7200 from infra/env.sh.
# SHVLA_SIM_TIMEOUT=
